{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he shall turn</b> — as in the manner of 'I shall give you a different heart' [and the like], the opposite of 'a son who disgraces his father.' And behold, all of them shall be of one heart to return to HaShem, fathers and children, before the great day comes. And now I conclude this commentary on this book. Regarding Elijah we find that he was in the days of Ahaziah — 'one to return to HaShem, fathers and children' — the son of Ahab. And we find written that Jehoram son of Ahab and Jehoshaphat inquired of Elisha the prophet, and it is written there: 'Here is Elisha son of Shaphat, who poured water on the hands of Elijah' — and this is a sign that he had already gone up in the storm to heaven, for the verse does not say 'who pours water.' Furthermore: Elisha did not separate from Elijah after he served him until his ascent. And behold, we find after the death of Jehoshaphat, in the days of Ahaziah his son, written: 'And there came to him a letter from Elijah the prophet' — and this indicates that then he wrote and sent it to him, whereas had it been written before his ascent it would have said 'and there was found' or 'and there was brought to him a letter that Elijah left.' And there is no doubt that in the days of our holy sages he was seen, and HaShem in His mercy will hasten his prophecy and speed the end of his coming."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The running text contains no punctuation; I have inserted quotation marks and em dashes to mark the Biblical citations and parenthetical glosses, but the reading 'one to return to HaShem, fathers and children' as a description of Ahaziah son of Ahab is textually difficult and may be corrupt. The phrase 'and HaShem in His mercies will hasten his prophecy' is ambiguous — 'his prophecy' could also read 'his vision' — but I have translated literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:28.870805357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}